     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">Can someone point me towards a </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">working</span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> example where </span><a href=\"https://rstudio.github.io/packrat/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rstudio.github.io/packrat/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0iGX_Yc8hXdMJ30TxEM6YD\">packrat</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> is used with </span><a href=\"https://ci.appveyor.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ci.appveyor.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3xe1jztgH0RWmHSjI1H6-M\">AppVeyor</a> or Travis-CI<span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">to build an R package? Searching through Google and GitHub, I can&#39;t find any packrat-enable package that uses AppVeyor.  For Travis, </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">I&#39;ve found a few </span><a href=\"https://github.com/richfitz/wood/blob/master/.travis.yml\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/richfitz/wood/blob/master/.travis.yml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1fSEy1u7Tt9b2J2BzFgqrj\">examples</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> that use @craig-citro &#39;s initial </span><a href=\"https://github.com/craigcitro/r-travis\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/craigcitro/r-travis&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0FxvBm0jGJDW1Xoi81eL6W\">r-travis</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> approach, but I&#39;d like to start this package with the newer approach of </span><a href=\"http://docs.travis-ci.com/user/languages/r/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.travis-ci.com/user/languages/r/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2M5KiZWiZ3s-JCpajuSfh_\">native R support</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">.</span></font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"><font size=\"2\"><br></font></span></div><div><p style=\"clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"><font size=\"2\">Do the yaml files need to change? Are there some settings I need to add through the Travis/AppVeyor websites?  </font><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">I have a very minimal package (</span><code style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">testthat</code><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">is the only dependency) that broke Travis &amp; AppVeyor builds. Here is the</span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><a href=\"https://github.com/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/tree/f110944be3e1b02d53ffbe69b71fc5d2d9dd6615\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/tree/f110944be3e1b02d53ffbe69b71fc5d2d9dd6615&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08Kn-3-134NsJTkTz30gI0\">code frozen for that commit</a><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">. </span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">Here is the </span><a href=\"https://travis-ci.org/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/builds/60886183\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://travis-ci.org/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/builds/60886183&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1lQxvJw0WOynglukh6Q3IE\">Travis-CI log</a><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">; h</span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">ere is the</span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><a href=\"https://ci.appveyor.com/project/wibeasley/premiss/build/1.0.10\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ci.appveyor.com/project/wibeasley/premiss/build/1.0.10&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1PdXzV5PXcF0r_Uv-xo3c8\">AppVeyor log</a><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">.</span></p></div><div><font size=\"2\">Since RStudio developers created Packrat, and advocate GitHub and CI, I thought I could find more examples of the two components working together in the same Package.</font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\">Two weeks ago I posted these questions separately in StackOverflow without much response.  I earned a StackOverflow <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/help/badges/63/tumbleweed\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/help/badges/63/tumbleweed&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ddbHb59237kgxcoDe6WoK\">tumbleweed</a> badge.</font></div><ul><li><font size=\"2\"><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29997095/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-travis-ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29997095/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-travis-ci&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2wY5BJmOk5Bc3ktnSD2GG1\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29997095/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-travis-ci</a></font></li><li><font size=\"2\"><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29996468/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-appveyor\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29996468/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-appveyor&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323861000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vzksuJLbC0bC_LSm8MFP8\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29996468/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-appveyor</a></font><br></li></ul><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\">Thanks, Will</span></font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
