    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>After much trial and error and further reading, it seems that this will do it, with a `.travis.yml` file like this:</div><div><br></div><div>    # R for travis: see documentation at <a href=\"https://docs.travis-ci.com/user/languages/r\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://docs.travis-ci.com/user/languages/r&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ooLQUdeASo8-VINMkhNZS\">https://docs.travis-ci.com/user/languages/r</a></div><div>    </div><div>    language: R</div><div>    sudo: false</div><div>    cache: packages</div><div>    install:</div><div>      - R -e &quot;0&quot; --args --bootstrap-packrat</div><div>    warnings_are_errors: false</div><div><br></div><div>The key lines in the above file are:</div><div><br></div><div>    install:</div><div>      - R -e &quot;0&quot; --args --bootstrap-packrat</div><div><br></div><div>This will start R, and builds the R packages in the local packrat directory so that they are available in the Travis machine. </div><div><br></div><div>After that, travis will continue and attempt to build the package, and will not need contact CRAN to get the dependencies because they are already available (assuming packrat is working as expected).</div><div><br></div><div>I discovered this trick here: <a href=\"https://travis-ci.org/ChowHub/paper-pattern-similarity/builds/127262823\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://travis-ci.org/ChowHub/paper-pattern-similarity/builds/127262823&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ihOXMJxU4jes-78WvhSFA\">https://travis-ci.org/ChowHub/paper-pattern-similarity/builds/127262823</a> and at <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/packrat/issues/158\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/packrat/issues/158&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3NTRa_oub8suh3DTf81IYO\">https://github.com/rstudio/packrat/issues/158</a>. I&#39;ve got it working here: <a href=\"https://travis-ci.org/benmarwick/mjbtramp/builds/157747326\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://travis-ci.org/benmarwick/mjbtramp/builds/157747326&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JqzV6YA4jJDMnAXczw5Ry\">https://travis-ci.org/benmarwick/mjbtramp/builds/157747326</a></div><div><br></div><div>The **advantage** of this is we can build on travis with the exact same packages that we&#39;re using locally. We don&#39;t have to get the latest packages from CRAN when we build on travis, now we can have more control of the package versions that travis builds with in our project. </div><div><br></div><div>The **disadvantage** is that the build time on travis is substantially increased. One of my projects went from 2-3 mins to 13-15 mins after switching to packrat. </div><div><br></div><div>Cross-posted from my Q&amp;A at <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/a/39338706/1036500\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/a/39338706/1036500&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3wI8caY8TIXSHD857bCgmI\">http://stackoverflow.com/a/39338706/1036500</a></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>On Thursday, August 18, 2016 at 6:50:26 AM UTC-7, Ben Marwick wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">This is a good question, I also want to know a simple way to make this work. Did you make any progress?<div><br></div><div>All I&#39;ve found so far is the example at<span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:19.5px\"> </span><a href=\"https://github.com/richfitz/wood/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:15px;color:rgb(0,89,153);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/richfitz/wood/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2orrYPNJI8VhB2fa68uGRx\">richfitz/wood</a>, but that looks more complex than what I think I need. I&#39;ve also asked this on SO just now: <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/q/39009579/1036500\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/q/39009579/1036500&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw01tjBBSI2fROc_jSSX2gIC\">http://stackoverflow.com/q/39009579/1036500</a><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:19.5px\"> </span><br><br>On Thursday, May 14, 2015 at 1:13:52 PM UTC+10, William Beasley wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">Can someone point me towards a </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">working</span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> example where </span><a href=\"https://rstudio.github.io/packrat/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rstudio.github.io/packrat/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vSX2ItMaC5ROileqkUAox\">packrat</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> is used with </span><a href=\"https://ci.appveyor.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ci.appveyor.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3EXUxBO-4rA5olMXVj6B_z\">AppVeyor</a> or Travis-CI<span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">to build an R package? Searching through Google and GitHub, I can&#39;t find any packrat-enable package that uses AppVeyor.  For Travis, </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">I&#39;ve found a few </span><a href=\"https://github.com/richfitz/wood/blob/master/.travis.yml\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/richfitz/wood/blob/master/.travis.yml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0n8LA6T_gN8bC1dhCBmsnA\">examples</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> that use @craig-citro &#39;s initial </span><a href=\"https://github.com/craigcitro/r-travis\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/craigcitro/r-travis&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2fKRz_nMCZSjvxrUiqthyV\">r-travis</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> approach, but I&#39;d like to start this package with the newer approach of </span><a href=\"http://docs.travis-ci.com/user/languages/r/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.travis-ci.com/user/languages/r/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0a4IOumPZUs0EedQw29jZV\">native R support</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">.</span></font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"><font size=\"2\"><br></font></span></div><div><p style=\"clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"><font size=\"2\">Do the yaml files need to change? Are there some settings I need to add through the Travis/AppVeyor websites?  </font><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">I have a very minimal package (</span><code style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">testthat</code><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">is the only dependency) that broke Travis &amp; AppVeyor builds. Here is the</span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><a href=\"https://github.com/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/tree/f110944be3e1b02d53ffbe69b71fc5d2d9dd6615\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/tree/f110944be3e1b02d53ffbe69b71fc5d2d9dd6615&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw05Yd5r3jsfmngGdZ9bauMf\">code frozen for that commit</a><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">. </span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">Here is the </span><a href=\"https://travis-ci.org/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/builds/60886183\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://travis-ci.org/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/builds/60886183&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3u2pLE5ACDCNVWBA5CXnlK\">Travis-CI log</a><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">; h</span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">ere is the</span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><a href=\"https://ci.appveyor.com/project/wibeasley/premiss/build/1.0.10\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ci.appveyor.com/project/wibeasley/premiss/build/1.0.10&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw393fbKhWcMq3I0IhtTkBPU\">AppVeyor log</a><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">.</span></p></div><div><font size=\"2\">Since RStudio developers created Packrat, and advocate GitHub and CI, I thought I could find more examples of the two components working together in the same Package.</font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\">Two weeks ago I posted these questions separately in StackOverflow without much response.  I earned a StackOverflow <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/help/badges/63/tumbleweed\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/help/badges/63/tumbleweed&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_Ddj6aPoka6FoFUuQvPvY\">tumbleweed</a> badge.</font></div><ul><li><font size=\"2\"><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29997095/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-travis-ci\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29997095/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-travis-ci&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2MRkHQXH79x_Ry7lSIoM1r\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29997095/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-travis-ci</a></font></li><li><font size=\"2\"><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29996468/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-appveyor\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29996468/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-appveyor&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323869000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nyenurEQUj1diHQeZ8bxR\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29996468/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-appveyor</a></font><br></li></ul><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\">Thanks, Will</span></font></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "bIw1o8iPDwAJ",
   "from": "Ben Marwick",
   "author": "b96d728b1b05f3e1",
   "date": "2016-09-15T04:31:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: Using Packrat with Travis-CI and AppVeyor",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve also got this working for appveyor, the solution here is similar to the [same question for Travis-CI](<a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/39009579/using-r-package-source-files-in-packrat-rather-than-cran-with-travis-ci?rq=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/39009579/using-r-package-source-files-in-packrat-rather-than-cran-with-travis-ci?rq%3D1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323872000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2fv6rBc9RoKZ_AnppQ6dB_\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/39009579/using-r-package-source-files-in-packrat-rather-than-cran-with-travis-ci?rq=1</a>). <div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s an example of an `appveyor.yml` file that will enable you to use packrat packages in your package:</div><div><br></div><div>    # DO NOT CHANGE the &quot;init&quot; and &quot;install&quot; sections below</div><div>    </div><div>    # Download script file from GitHub</div><div>    init:</div><div>      ps: |</div><div>            $ErrorActionPreference = &quot;Stop&quot;</div><div>            Invoke-WebRequest <a href=\"http://raw.github.com/krlmlr/r-appveyor/master/scripts/appveyor-tool.ps1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://raw.github.com/krlmlr/r-appveyor/master/scripts/appveyor-tool.ps1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323872000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2TU4HeMDnNjLl1D7MzPHpc\">http://raw.github.com/krlmlr/r-appveyor/master/scripts/appveyor-tool.ps1</a> -OutFile &quot;..\\appveyor-tool.ps1&quot;</div><div>            Import-Module &#39;..\\appveyor-tool.ps1&#39;</div><div>    install:</div><div>      ps: Bootstrap</div><div>    </div><div>    # Adapt as necessary starting from here</div><div>    </div><div>    environment:</div><div>      global:</div><div>       WARNINGS_ARE_ERRORS: 0</div><div>       USE_RTOOLS: true</div><div>    </div><div>    build_script:</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>      - R -e  &quot;0&quot; --args --bootstrap-packrat</div><div>    </div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>    test_script:</div><div>      - travis-tool.sh run_tests</div><div>    </div><div>    on_failure:</div><div>      - 7z a failure.zip *.Rcheck\\*</div><div>      - appveyor PushArtifact failure.zip</div><div>    </div><div>    artifacts:</div><div>      - path: &#39;*.Rcheck\\**\\*.log&#39;</div><div>        name: Logs</div><div>    </div><div>      - path: &#39;*.Rcheck\\**\\*.out&#39;</div><div>        name: Logs</div><div>    </div><div>      - path: &#39;*.Rcheck\\**\\*.fail&#39;</div><div>        name: Logs</div><div>    </div><div>      - path: &#39;*.Rcheck\\**\\*.Rout&#39;</div><div>        name: Logs</div><div>    </div><div>      - path: &#39;\\*_*.tar.gz&#39;</div><div>        name: Bits</div><div>    </div><div>      - path: &#39;\\*_*.zip&#39;</div><div>        name: Bits</div><div><br></div><div>The important parts that differ from [the template](<a href=\"https://github.com/krlmlr/r-appveyor/blob/master/sample.appveyor.yml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/krlmlr/r-appveyor/blob/master/sample.appveyor.yml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323872000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2KKGHPtD68gfcf3nMh_Xxz\">https://github.com/krlmlr/r-appveyor/blob/master/sample.appveyor.yml</a>) are:</div><div><br></div><div>     environment:</div><div>          global:</div><div>           WARNINGS_ARE_ERRORS: 0</div><div>           USE_RTOOLS: true</div><div>        </div><div>        build_script:</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>          - R -e  &quot;0&quot; --args --bootstrap-packrat</div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>This enables Rtools for the build, and loads the packrat packages.</div><div><br></div><div>It&#39;s also important to note that we are excluding ` - travis-tool.sh install_deps` because that would cause the packages you depend on to be downloaded from CRAN, rather than built from your packrat directory. </div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s an example of an appveyor build for a simple R package where this is working: <a href=\"https://ci.appveyor.com/project/benmarwick/javaonappveyortest/build/1.0.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ci.appveyor.com/project/benmarwick/javaonappveyortest/build/1.0.21&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323872000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LHr--9q3iLMAJLJIfDQcz\">https://ci.appveyor.com/project/benmarwick/javaonappveyortest/build/1.0.21</a></div><div><br></div><div>cross-posted from SO: <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/a/39503140/1036500\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/a/39503140/1036500&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323872000&amp;usg=AOvVaw009lVLU1ICpJ-zUEdy2t9a\">http://stackoverflow.com/a/39503140/1036500</a></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Wednesday, May 13, 2015 at 8:13:52 PM UTC-7, William Beasley wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">Can someone point me towards a </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">working</span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> example where </span><a href=\"https://rstudio.github.io/packrat/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rstudio.github.io/packrat/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2RgZWkXx4q6Epd38rB9hIh\">packrat</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> is used with </span><a href=\"https://ci.appveyor.com/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ci.appveyor.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1iagSg-CuvASbKhScLVqoE\">AppVeyor</a> or Travis-CI<span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">to build an R package? Searching through Google and GitHub, I can&#39;t find any packrat-enable package that uses AppVeyor.  For Travis, </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">I&#39;ve found a few </span><a href=\"https://github.com/richfitz/wood/blob/master/.travis.yml\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/richfitz/wood/blob/master/.travis.yml&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3mBJPcuVTh6_2RfYbQILvb\">examples</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> that use @craig-citro &#39;s initial </span><a href=\"https://github.com/craigcitro/r-travis\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/craigcitro/r-travis&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1o9yy-yV32CfVrWvuCTLs9\">r-travis</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> approach, but I&#39;d like to start this package with the newer approach of </span><a href=\"http://docs.travis-ci.com/user/languages/r/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165);font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.travis-ci.com/user/languages/r/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw06vg4qcQqkWOOk5AuPUSsr\">native R support</a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">.</span></font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"><font size=\"2\"><br></font></span></div><div><p style=\"clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"><font size=\"2\">Do the yaml files need to change? Are there some settings I need to add through the Travis/AppVeyor websites?  </font><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">I have a very minimal package (</span><code style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(238,238,238)\">testthat</code><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">is the only dependency) that broke Travis &amp; AppVeyor builds. Here is the</span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><a href=\"https://github.com/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/tree/f110944be3e1b02d53ffbe69b71fc5d2d9dd6615\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/tree/f110944be3e1b02d53ffbe69b71fc5d2d9dd6615&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1hyQW8iLYsEIyxkQELEcEC\">code frozen for that commit</a><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">. </span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">Here is the </span><a href=\"https://travis-ci.org/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/builds/60886183\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://travis-ci.org/OuhscBbmc/Premiss/builds/60886183&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2BxC9d2VO78xLgYcsH3iGL\">Travis-CI log</a><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">; h</span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">ere is the</span><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\"> </span><a href=\"https://ci.appveyor.com/project/wibeasley/premiss/build/1.0.10\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px;color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ci.appveyor.com/project/wibeasley/premiss/build/1.0.10&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3f7nPJmoA54-aQvUeIWBG2\">AppVeyor log</a><span style=\"font-size:small;line-height:17.7272720336914px\">.</span></p></div><div><font size=\"2\">Since RStudio developers created Packrat, and advocate GitHub and CI, I thought I could find more examples of the two components working together in the same Package.</font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\">Two weeks ago I posted these questions separately in StackOverflow without much response.  I earned a StackOverflow <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/help/badges/63/tumbleweed\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/help/badges/63/tumbleweed&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2XUElXkH9PXms31qwDz7fR\">tumbleweed</a> badge.</font></div><ul><li><font size=\"2\"><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29997095/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-travis-ci\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29997095/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-travis-ci&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0mbuH7vknnoMIOfAFnTJ-s\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29997095/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-travis-ci</a></font></li><li><font size=\"2\"><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29996468/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-appveyor\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29996468/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-appveyor&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242323873000&amp;usg=AOvVaw13o7aU7rnfpDOXb51IKwBg\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29996468/building-r-packages-with-packrat-and-appveyor</a></font><br></li></ul><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:17px\">Thanks, Will</span></font></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
